{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/132931-cwod-post-apocalypse-action-game-home-brew","id":132931,"title":"cWOD Post-Apocalypse action game home brew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-11T17:36:26-07:00","id":132931,"title":"cWOD Post-Apocalypse action game home brew","content":"so my friend and I are trying to come up with a WOD where the world and supernaturals survived the time of judgement. its pretty well converted to the exalted second ed. system because its our belief with the aftermath of Gehenna, the Apocalypse, and the fall of the Gauntlet people's are much more willing to accept the grim reality. and we like the stunt system and D.V.s. makes combat way quicker. I was just curious about any suggestions. the goal is a crossover friendly system with smooth combat that doesn't sacrifice the narrative appeal of the originals, with a focus on action adventure, dark beauty , romance and drama. this isn't Interview with a Vampire, this is more Underworld/ Matrix/Resident Evil movies style of play and action. so its not really the same animal so i ask that judge it on its own merits. <br /> <b>the fluff: What's happening in the setting</b><br /> <br /> <b>theme:</b> Life on the brink: society, while not in ruins is most certainly on the verge. humanity got a good hard look at the real world and dosn't know what to do. many desperatly try to carry on find that when you've lived a lie your whole life, its simply not good enough when the truth sneaks up and bites you on the neck. everyday new security measures are added to the day to day lives of ordinary people and more and more society starts to fully grasp what it has not only lost but never really had to begin with. many despair at their powerlessness and many rage against the creatures who would dare challenge them as masters of their own fate. Saftey, or at least the illusion of it becomes a valueable thing and many cling to any bastion of stability they can. every day a new attrocity of eldritch horror is unleashed is another straw upon the camel's back. sooner or later its going to be one too many and the whole charade is going to come crashing down around everybody's ears. But these are the times when we are truly tested. human kind is really learning how strong it actually is in the face of the deepest darkness. Strength among weakness, hope among wreckage, action among fear, so utterly...human.<br /> <br /> <b>Mood: </b> Paranoia and Purpose: Nobody trusts anybody and everybody has an agenda. <br /> <br /> Mortals: after the shit hit the fan, life in most corners of the earth has continued but in a post tramatic oh my god there are things out there that can kill me at any given moment kind of way. the majority of people in WOD have always had some kind of nameless fear running through back burners of their brains but now the blinders are off and they KNOW something is out their. but the fact that supernaturals are relatively rare and coupled with the fact that they have existed alongside humanity for centuries leaves them with a quandary. many are arguing for civil rights. Many more are finding out that friends, coworkers and loved ones are infact something else. while most are horrified at the idea don't forget that its easy to hate a group where you don't know anyone. its another to hate someone you've known for years hasn't specifically hurt you and your family or comes to Christmas dinner. <br /> This has played absolute Hell with the Economy. many movers and shakers died in the recent apocalypse or were outed as vampires or mages running a world wide conspiracy placing many legitimate business on the official chopping block. the government isn't much better off as the sheer depth of supernatural infestation into virtually every power structure shocks and dismays most of the freeworld leading to an almost total system collapse. Think of it like the hydra infiltration of shield but on a massive world wide level. soon their are riots and martial law and many many people go insane. then there are the...things happening. Zombie hordes, dragons appearing across the sky, mages hurling fireballs over Manhattan and spirits running amok. while cities aren't left in ruin and rubble many are damn close. people adopt a siege mentality no one knows who to trust or even what to think. But it also speaks volumes of the resiliency and adaptability of the human mind that it hasn't driven them over the collective edge. despite appearances mankind has not collapsed utterly but it appears that it may be entering a new dark age after the fall of the old. but also a new age of wonder and excitement. in many ways the human race feels and acts more alive and aware than they have in millennia. like the world crashing down around them was really the kick in the pants they needed to get up and move again.<br /> <b>Vampire:</b> <br /> <br /> the ancients did rise but we through out the withering. instead their rise sent the elders into a blood frenzy ala the week of nightmares. The Ancients themselves never arose physically as such but rather gorged themselves by proxy their children. leaving only the youngest vampires sane enough to get to hiding. the masquerade barely hangs by a thread. too many inexperienced<br /> <br /> vampires roam the night with out connections and influence to cover their tracks and every night some new gadget comes along with improved video and communication tech to expose them. the camerillia has fallen and Anarchs and upstarts rule the streets in the once safe havens of stability. The sabbat revels in the chaos but have lost much of their strength as well.<br /> Meanwhile the inquistion is circualing ever closer and all it'll take is one vamp to f**k up and blow the whole cover. then one day some one does, suddenly the once proud kindread are running for their unlives. in world where heat signature apps are on every smart phone and suspension on everyone's mind. <br /> but if Kindred are good at anything, its operating unseen and making the world work to its advantage. the stakes are high and the game is set. stay hidden, infiltrate, take over and rule the night.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b> the garou did the impossible, they prevented the rise of the wyrm. bringing together the ferra and forming an alliance with human mages, the shapeshifters were able to prevent the asension of the wyrm and bind it into slumber. they could not destroy it without dooming the gaia to fate worse than death, but they were victorious upon their field of battle. the cost was great and the battle was hard but it was won. the wyrm fell upon the fields of the apocalypse and its forces were driven back. more than that they managed to do something even more, they survived. the apocalypse war is over. gaia now has time to heal and recover from her wounds and for the first time in a generation, new garou are being born. more curiously is that more and more metis are being born without deformities. the shapeshifters of the world indeed have many reasons to rejoice.except one small hitch, Humanity. it hasn't stopped. the managed to bind the anthropomorphic personification of destruction and corruption, but the victory that they fought so hard for could all be undone unless something is done about the throngs and throngs of humans. realizing very quickly that they have indeed only alleviated the symptoms rather than cure the disease the ferra of the world are now at an impasse. do they repeat the mistakes of the past of do they find new ways to save the world? <br /> <br /> <b>Mage:</b> the ascension war was a lie. the world cannot and never will be forced to ascend. when the fires of judgment came humanity took one look at it and said, no. not yet. in many ways it was just another form of control, the technocracy and traditions alike trying to tell humanity what was right, what was wrong, how to live how to think, run don't walk, be like us not like them, I'm right your wrong. well humanity made its choice. it said sure, we'll have wonder, but we'll do it our way. the technocracy has been hit hard. between its own infighting and exposure to the general populace, finds the institutions it helped create and build suddenly turn against it. N.W.O. agents brought before senate committees and progenitors arrested for violating the Geneva conventions. while it still stands the influence and power it once took for granted is now fading quickly. it must now for the first time work for and with humanity than against them. the traditions while tickled pink at the fate befallen their rivals in no better condition. while their magic is certainly easier, the general populace looks at them with same deadly twinkle it had during the burning times. marauders no longer barred from reality outright roam the landscape like storms sweeping away entire towns with their madness and the dark nephandi are still out there. they have been in this place before and see this as a brave new world which only needs the slightest of pushes to shatter into tiny pieces.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling:</b> the Mists have not fallen, but they have changed. upon the collapse of the gauntlet, an upsurge of glamor has all but crippled the forces of banality. for the first time in millenia, the fae are feel truely whole. what was once hollow dreams becomes stark reality, and the majesty of arcaida now lives again on earth. then why the fae wonder, have the gates to their home not open again? are they well and truely banished? furthermore the rift between noble and commoner has not healed and the dark kin always out there lurking in the shadows of nightmare. further complicating matters is the fae must now contend with mortal politics. the fae have always seen themselves as apart from the mortal world, but now the world accepts their existence because it must (once you see a griffin trot down main street the fact your secretary is secretly an elf seems the least of your problems). hardly saints by any stretch of the word, the fae have always had their share of monsters and murderers and it seems they must now step extra lively or face the same fate as some of the other creatures of the world of darkness. for their part fae remember the human parts of their lives quite well and don't necessarily want to abandon them. after all many had human spouses, children and friends and though their lives had banality also special moments of pure and powerful glamor. the small moments like a private joke and seeing your child walk for the first time and how good it felt to FINALLY get that promotion. things you just don't find in the fae world. HUMAN things.<br /> <br /> Wraith: the underworld is gone. broken beyond repair by the maelstrom. as a result the dead have have no where to go but to stay on earth. this is pretty much the least developed one we have. the world seems to be over run no one knows what to do about them fortunately, the vast majority are unable to interact with the world around them and despite the comparitve lack of gauntlet, most people simply can't see ghosts, we are thinking about incorporating shadowlands into the setting but mostlly we've been focusing on the settings above.<br /> <br /> Spirits: during the apocalypse the gauntlet fell allowing spirits and material beings to interact on a massive scale for the first time in eons. while the umbra has NOT merged with the material world, its there, and if your not careful, you'll fall in. there are patches where it has repaired itsself, (the weaver still functions though the binding of the wyrm has diminished her power as well) but compared to what it was its thinnest of layers. <br /> <br /> the others: we have no plans to add Demon the Fallen, Hunter the Reckoning , Mummy the Resurrection, or Kindred of the East anytime soon, though KOE is a possibility if we have a mind to do so. its mostly just a matter of time.<br /> <br /> <b>the crunch: rule changes </b><br /> <br /> unlike exalted/scion we do not allow people to move every tick with out a supernatural power.<br /> <br /> we kept the original clans/traditions/kiths/tribes from cWOD rather than nWOD. <br /> <br /> using exalted abilities we replaced Archery with Firearms, War with Tactics, Lore with Academics, Sail with Drive, and Ride with Animal Ken<br /> <br /> we use the D.V. and M.D.V. and Soak systems from exalted<br /> <br /> we have most disciplines and gifts converted, sphere magick remains pretty much the same expect what counts as coincidental and vulgar has changed slightly to accommodate a more lenient consensus.<br /> <br /> we got rid of generation in favor of requiem's blood potency trait, the antediluvians are simply vampires who through ancient and arcane arts lost to time have managed to hold their powers through torpor. we're going the poof method on this. it simply always was. <br /> <br /> all roles are at a base target number of seven. tens count as two on all roles unless stated otherwise.<br /> on a similar note we would gave every splat a &quot;power trait&quot; similiar to Nwod but kept most of the original flavors from old world. (Mages have Arete, Changelings have Glamor, Though with werewolves we are leaning more toward Primal Urge as it seems like a handy combo between Rage and Gnosis)<br /> <br /> fuel traits (like blood points and quintessence are much higher similar to Essence motes in exalted.<br /> <br /> every clan/tribe/tradition/kith ect. has a clan boon that is an inborn trait. for example: brujah can spend a will power and count tens twice on damage or add their blood potency to social roles. ect.<br /> <br /> every splat gets what's called a unique augment: a way to boost their abilities to achieve superhuman feats as a side effect<br /> Vampires may add dice to their attributes up to double but only for scene. (vampires typically have a smaller fuel trait BP x ten, plus the advantage of their disciplines)<br /> Werewolves: can add their power trait to their own die pool, or the pool of their pack mate on a mote for die basis. coupled with their shifting it packs a wollop<br /> Mages: can lower the target number of their role down to four or spend four quint and wp and turn all die in their pool as success<br /> Changelings: creatures of unbridled passions can spend a glamor in place of a willpower to use a virtue channel and typically have higher virtues.<br /> <br /> <br /> we kept the masquerade clans but got rid of Caitiff, all kindred have a clan lineage even if they can't identify it, they are for all metaphysical and practical purposes a member of that clan. (caitiff just never made much sense to us so we dumped it)<br /> <br /> Paradox has easied a bit, though the consensus has not yet drifted to the point where wonders are fully acceptable. its more a matter of scale than plausability. many willing to accept a person can throw a fire ball, few are willing to accept that a person can turn a city into cotton candy. furthermore science and reason still hold a lot of power. people are willing to accept the fantastic not because its magic, but because they just haven't figured out how it works yet. but given time...<br /> <br /> Banality still exists a nine to five is a nine to five cubicle hell is still a cubicle hell, but it lost the power to destroy the fae, now fae must contend with too much glamor and risk looking their human sides. (we wanted a way that changeling could walk into a room with a werewolf or a vampire, still have the vampire scary to the changeling but not so overwhelmed by them in terms of sheer power that they are completely outmatched. besides we never liked the concept of banality anyways so we got rid of it as game device.<br /> <br /> We use a modified limit system from exalted because its a good hinderence on monsters and supernaturals. each monster has different limits and gains it in different ways.<br /> <br /> the gauntlet is much thinner here. typically -4 from its old rating expect in places where it specifically and deliberately raised through magical or super science measures. so lots and lots and lots of shallowings.<br /> <br /> <b>What we're stuck on.</b><br /> <br /> General<br /> mostly setting details as to how shit hit the fan and what got wrecked and how, i've got a pretty good idea for america and canada but the world is a big place and ideas as to how magic becoming visible to the rest of the world and their reactions would be great. like how would brazil handle it? japan? russia? that kind of thing. <br /> <br /> Vampire: <br /> a good old fashioned frenzy system that works for both vampires and werewolves and anyone with the berzerker merit or short fuse flaw. something that's easy to understand and use in game. it needs to have teeth if its going to be effective but we need the ability to use get through a game with out everyone tearing each other to pieces.<br /> <br /> a good way to handle sunlight, (I'm thinking one aggravated damage every three ticks but this Fortitude presents something of a problem.)<br /> <br /> we're debating whether to handle health levels the old way, the exalted way or the new world way,<br /> <br /> Changeling:<br /> changeling is the hardest sell to my group so i came up with a new magic the arts and realms systems as written seems a bit, limited, too limited for a setting like this, trying to come up with something more free form and similar to mage with out copy pasting it.<br /> <br /> we want to avoid Demon the fallen as written because it just seems both too powerful and too limiting in its fluff. I'm all for judo-christian angels and demons but it just seems there should be more than that. in my opinion it also lacks the human element that makes WOD so great. we've been kicking around ideas for a Nephlim character type but are having trouble getting a good grasp as to what Angels and Demons are. i'm not trying to steal any one's ideas so if someone can point me to a good reference to angelic/demonic beings from different cultures around the world that would be great.<br /> <br /> we would like a way that makes Glamor faster to get, they can do so by being wounderous themselves, with stunts but otherwise as it stands it takes several dramatic actions over the course of several scenes to gain any except from dross. any ideas?<br /> <br /> for you exalted players out there, zombie hordes seems born for mass combat but we find the rules in exalted to be a little clunky, any ideas or references to simplified rules?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T19:19:57-07:00","id":133049,"title":"","content":"When loooking for fae who. interact with mortals and who have a more impressive magic system look no further than dark ages fae. Unless you want to go a bit mad and use all the errata and graceful wicked masks. But ya dark ages fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T02:56:19-07:00","id":144325,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, I want to do a cWoD postapocalyptic setting too, but a one that happens before Time of Judgement. Is it a crossover of Neuroshima (a postnuclear RP created in my country) and cWoD, in essence.<br /> <br /> I have little time to put on everything on paper here, so I will just state few things.<br /> <br /> Masquerade, Veil et cetera are undone. Humans know about vampires and shapeshifters. Delirium is lessened in effect because mundanes who survived the events that cause the world to be the way it is have seen worst shit than 9 feet tall humanoid wolves. <br /> <br /> Setting in former USA. The country in shambles, with few countries larger than city-states. Republic of New York, Texas and Appalachian Confederation are those which the size of a former state. Among major city-states are Las Vegas, Salt Lake City, Miami and Detroit, though the two last are barely civilized due to various reasons.<br /> <br /> Forget about Sabbat and Camarilla, local Sects are in shambles. Mexico City is long gobbled by Neojungle, an ecologic experiment gone wrong and reeking of rampant Wyld. Even shifters avoid the place, for its alien enviroment is dangerous for Gaian lifeforms. In the North, American Midwest is gobbled by sentient industrial complex that is similarly went out of countrol and is slowly, but firmly expanding at the cost of human territories. Possibly Weaver tainted. What is left of Sabbat maintains presence in Miami and Detroit, and ruling openly of some of humans and clashing with other survivors. The leftover Kindred are trying to blend with survivors, something hiding their true nature, sometimes being vampires openly if the local mentality is basically &quot;s/he drinks blood, but at least is not fucking machine from the North&quot;. <br /> <br /> Garou Nation and other local shifters suffered badly, and of Garou least affected Tribes were &quot;Pure Tribes&quot; and Red Talons. Their immediate concern is to stop 'Weaver-spawns' from encroaching further, and there are doubts what to do about the new alien ecosystem encroaching from the South.<br /> <br /> With the fall of civilization Technocracy, except for Void Engineers who maintain outposts in Umbra, is in pieces. Remaining Technocratic Mages, Virtual Adepts, Sons of Ether and even Glasswalkers joined with whatever remained of American military, trying to stop encroaching machines and preserve what they can of human civilization. The alliance is tenuous, grudges surfacing, but they have to keep cooperating to have even a sliver of hope.<br /> <br /> But what made civilization fall in the first place? Ratkin finally unleashed their Birthing Plague, trying to topple human civilization. Old World was affected the most by the Plague, but in the New World it had devestating effect, but not as expected by wererats. Local humanity survived the plague, though vampires were badly affected by sudden drop of available juicebags.<br /> <br /> (I gotta go, I will continue later on. Tell me if it is not haphazard, I'm basically trying to merge two different settings).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T23:49:48-07:00","id":146465,"title":"","content":"I like the Idea of a neojungle. Wyld energies birthing something alien and hostile toward earthly life. and that sentient City eating the midwest? that would be bad as that's my back yard... it sounds a lot like the God Machine but different enough. does it assimilate living organisms like the borg? could you imagine Garou borg assimiliating everything they can get their hands on? what if it assimilates a vampire and becomes a ghoul with vitae addiction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T02:44:05-07:00","id":146531,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> In Neuroshima, Moloch, as it was dubbed by the survivors, assimilated whole factories and industrial complexes, but for some reason experimented from time to time with kidnapping people and hooking their brains to machines. Or simply twisting them into mutants and releasing free, with no apparent reason and normal folks shunning them and even killing because of sheer paranoia they might be infiltrators. Some science minded survivors speculate it simply wants to learn about humans to better adapt to increasing resistance. To be always step ahead. <br /> <br /> As for Neojungle, in the original it was failed experiment to restore Amazon Jungle. For reasons unknown, it started propagating and changing enviroment to its own needs, spawning new lifeforms evolving at accelerated pace. It gobbled most of Mexico by now, and gained a minor foothold cut off from the main body in Florida (probably seeds propagating through air). Needless to say, Miami is in human control, but by mere relatively near presence of Neojungles most of them are mutants. Thankfully, their retain free will (as well as animals which mutated but strayed away from the enviroment which spawned them. People who can tame them can find them useful).<br /> <br /> As for your question, &quot;Moloch&quot; would just hook Garou's brain to a machine and do away with the body. Or just do something that would make Tzimisce blush and dump the poor sod somewhere. The latter which sounds counterproductive to what alleged Weaver influenced thing would do, but the experiments might have a reason behind it even if alien.<br /> <br /> As for a vampire, I'm not sure a brain would maintain its capacity without steady access to vitae or that undead body would be vulnerable to genetic engineering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}